A||||8||Taijiguy||Finally! Pics to dispell the romours!||||1||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||07-31-2000||06:21 PM||||OK, so I know some of you thought maybe I was a Ford motor company executive trolling these pages to gain technical information about Fieros for some secret special project. OK, well, here's proof that I really DO own a Fiero. Can I keep my membership now?? <P>Give the pics a minute to load.....<P>This is what we looked like before the facelift:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=964084&a=7454310&p=25373332&Sequence=0">    <P>Here's the engine; post rebuild. All injection components removed. Edelbrock performer manifold, Holley 390-4bbl etc.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=964084&a=7454310&p=25373138&Sequence=0">   <P>I couldn't wait to get home and glass this bad-boy in place. Thanks 007Doug!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=964084&a=7454310&p=25373140&Sequence=0">   <P>What have I DONE?? Prepping for piant. Pearl white with gray graphics. Still working on the scheme! Hope to lay paint this coming weekend!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=964084&a=7454310&p=25373139&Sequence=0">   <P>This is the Getrag 5 speed from a 92 Beretta. I used the original four speed brackets with sligh modification. I fabricated the bottom bracket that mounts the selctor lever. I used GM door hinge pin  (cut to length) and bronze bushings. They were a perfect fit! I also modified the Fiero slave to replace the original Beretta slave.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=964084&a=7454310&p=25375281&Sequence=0"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||HYPTNOTiSE||07-31-2000||07:03 PM||||is the carbed engine in and running? is the throttle linkage hooked up?  How'd did you work that?  Umm, is that a 2 barrel manifold with an adapter plate for 4 barrel or is it a 4 barrel manifold, any they still available?<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||07-31-2000||07:21 PM||||No, the motor isn't in place yet, but from what I can tell, the throttle linkage will be no problem. The intake is the two piece Edelbrock setup, with the 4bbl top. Someone here on the forum had the same setup for sale for 175 bucks, although you can buy them new for a few bucks more. Jegs and Summit each have the different parts. Jegs has the upper part,  and Summit has the lower part. I'm hoping to add a nitrous setup soon, after I recover from the fianancial crush of what I've done so far.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
