Z||000008||Taijiguy||08-01-2000||09:42 AM||||Hi Guys (and gals?)<P>The wing is gone, already sold. It had the 7" standoffs when I got the car, but they placed the wing where it COMPLETELY blocked the rear view. I cut them down to about 2 1/2", which gave it a cool profile. But I favored the IMSA, so that's why I went that route. <BR>I didn't post the pics, but I'm also in the process of glassing in Beretta headlights as well. I cut the headlight doors out, and increased the size of the openings, they'll fit primarily below the hood line, but there will be a slight rise in the hood right above the lights. Don't know if it'll work for sure, but I'm giving it a shot!<BR>The paint will be pearl white, with dark gray metallic airbrushed accents and striping. I'll also paint the wheels the same gray. For the most part it'll be mono'd, with all identifying marks removed (don't want anyone to know it's a Ford!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>As for power, with the cam profile I have, and the single plane manifold, along with other mods, Desktop Dyno indicates power should be around 200. I'll add <BR>nitrous in the next couple of months....<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
